  "question": {
    "text": "The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> of ammonium phosphate solution, if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pk</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> of phosphoric acid and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pk</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math> of ammonium hydroxide are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>23</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn></math> respectively, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is salt of weak acid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and weak base <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>pka</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>pkb</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p>",
